body:
> Before this change, UiState was merging the indexIds directly with the other state,

Not sure to understand the meaning of the comment. Could you explain? The current format of `uiState` is already the one described by @francoischalifour. I don't think we have to update its structure. The types inside the codebase are not up-to-date though, this is the idea:

```ts
type UiState = {
  [indexId: string]: IndexUiState;
};

const movies: IndexUiState = {
  query: "hammer"
};

const songs: IndexUiState = {
  query: "burning"
};

const uiState: UiState = {
  songs,
  movies
};
```
